{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When the base advances, a pushed merge commit can disclose the factory's identity in a discreet repository."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Enabling discreet mode mid-run can leave earlier branding and an internal dashboard URL in published commits or a landing report."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When two PRs share a head SHA, recovery can associate the run with the wrong PR and overwrite its body."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A large collision history absent from both records and refs causes sequential lookups that delay other repository work, but the search terminates."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An accepted custom prefix combined with a title can create an invalid branch name and cause the run to fail."},{"id":"F7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The reproduced generic review-status label does not identify the factory or establish a functional failure."}]}